+### `app.enableWebAuthnBrowserAuthenticator()` _macOS_
+
+Returns `boolean` - Enables Chromium's native browser passkey authenticator when
+supported by this process's macOS version and signed browser entitlement. Returns
+`false` without changing configuration when unavailable. Requires macOS 13.5 or
+later and Apple's managed `com.apple.developer.web-browser.public-key-credential`
+entitlement. This operation does not request access or enumerate credentials.
+
+Requests keep their original web origin and use Chromium's existing validation,
+extensions and native credential-provider UI. Browser and app-specific passkeys
+are modes of the same authenticator: enabling browser mode replaces app mode;
+explicitly setting `configureWebAuthn({ platformPasskeys: true })` selects app mode,
+and setting it to `false` disables either mode. Other omitted configuration stays
+unchanged, including Touch ID.
+
+When Touch ID is also configured, the existing `select-webauthn-authenticator`
+event identifies this authenticator as `platformPasskeys` and defaults to it when
+no listener is installed. Support does not imply that a matching credential exists
+or that the user will approve a request.
+
 ### `app.disableHardwareAcceleration()`

 Disables hardware acceleration for current app.
